{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1239187-spiritual-ascension-rote-1st-edition-m-taw","id":1239187,"title":"Spiritual Ascension Rote - 1st edition M:tAw","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-26T21:12:39-07:00","id":1239187,"title":"Spiritual Ascension Rote - 1st edition M:tAw","content":"Can anyone explain the full range of effects of the Spiritual Ascension rote from the Grimoire of Grimoires (page 86)?<br /> Does it dump you into Shadow (or twilight), or transform you in the Material?<br /> How does it affect movement?<br /> Can you physically affect the Material?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T23:06:41-07:00","id":1239202,"title":"","content":"It doesn't do anything to transport you, but while that means you wouldn't end up in the Shadow you probably would end up in Twilight (Though Twilight is a phase of reality rather than a place in it) as you have no Manifestations to maintain you in the Material. Though in 1e Manifestation worked a little differently, so you could probably pay the Mana or Essence cost to become physical if I'm remembering that correctly. Considering the way the spell is intended to be used (To make Gulmoths able to be trapped in the Codex) it probably also doesn't give you access to Numina or anything else a spirit might be able to do usually except be made of ephemera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T21:50:26-07:00","id":1239560,"title":"","content":"Unwinding Fleshly Bonds: \u201cSpiritual Ascension,\u201d<br /> (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022); Intelligence + Occult + Life; This<br /> spell works like the Forces spell \u201cFiery Transformation,\u201d<br /> save that instead of turning the caster into a creature<br /> of fre, it allows the caster to turn his physical body into<br /> spiritual ephemera. Unlike with the spell \u201cSpirit Road\u201d or<br /> similar magics, this is not simply transferring the body into<br /> Twilight or Shadow. This actually changes the form into<br /> spiritual essence. <br /> [At Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, this spell can be used on<br /> other physical creatures by touch, and was most often used<br /> by Gaolers to transform Abyssal intrusions with physical<br /> bodies into spiritual entities in order to imprison them<br /> within the Codex.]<br /> <br /> It should cause you to slip into twilight. Gravity no longer affects you. You can fly like other spirits. But - like with Fiery Transformation - planes of force allow you to interact with other things?<br /> <br /> This really needs a designer to clarify...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T23:05:07-07:00","id":1239569,"title":"","content":"Fiery Transformation allows you to interact with things by setting them on fire. I'm pretty sure you can't fly either as spirits don't fly unless they have wings or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T23:15:31-07:00","id":1239571,"title":"","content":"Strange. I thought entering the Shadow already transitions things into Spirit-aligned ephemera? I can\u2019t recall at the moment if that is the case, and if so whether Spirit spells can affect them as if they were spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T23:19:46-07:00","id":1239574,"title":"","content":"Yeah but that's a second edition thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T23:50:07-07:00","id":1239581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1239187-spiritual-ascension-rote-1st-edition-m-taw?p=1239574#post1239574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but that's a second edition thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually not. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> What the Spiritual Ascension spell does is make that transition without putting you in the Shadow, which is useful for the Gaolers since they'd hardly want to send their prey to a place that's also hostile to themselves while trying to make a capture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T07:21:47-07:00","id":1239669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1239187-spiritual-ascension-rote-1st-edition-m-taw?p=1239569#post1239569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fiery Transformation allows you to interact with things by setting them on fire. I'm pretty sure you can't fly either as spirits don't fly unless they have wings or something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, all spirits - by the fact of being unaffected by gravity - can sort of hover at speed, and even &quot;fly&quot; to a height that is related either to rank or one of their attributes (ie.: finesse).All of that is in the Book of Spirits...<br /> <br /> <b>Speed</b>: <br /> Speed is equal to Power + Finesse + a \u201cspecies factor.\u201d Spirits that take human or animal form have a species factor equal to their earthly counterpart, although Rank 1 spirits, especially of normally immobile things, are often unaware that they can move. Spirits of inanimate objects usually have a species factor equal to 0, while spirits of more abstract forms generally have a species factor of 10. Vehicle spirits often have Acceleration traits equal to their material cousins, rather than a Speed trait (see the World of Darkness Rulebook, p. 142). To fnd the maximum<br /> Speed, add the spirit\u2019s Power + Finesse to the physical counterpart\u2019s maximum Speed.<br /> <br /> <b>In Twilight, all spirits (even spirits without apparent appendages) are considered to be able to move in just about any direction. Even those without \u201cwings\u201d or association with the concept of \ufb02ight (air elementals) can hover in any direction \u2014 though without a clear connection to the concept of \ufb02ight, they must hover within their Speed (in yards) off the ground, or at least a solid surface. For the most part, they are not bound by gravity, or suffer its effects </b>\u2014 you can\u2019t \u201cpush\u201d a murder spirit in Twilight down an elevator shaft. Materialized spirits are quite physical. They are affected by gravity, for example. They can still move about, per their Speed trait, but unless they have \u201cwings\u201d or some such, they cannot \ufb02y. Those that don\u2019t have wheels, legs, tentacles or treads, for example, are assumed to hover just off the ground. <br /> <br /> <br /> Secondarily, besides setting things on fire... Fiery Transformation specifically mentions that &quot;planes of force&quot; allow the mage to interact with people and objects physically. So, said mage can grapple someone while burning them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","user":"DrKorpal","date":". 07-28-2018, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T07:30:30-07:00","id":1239671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1239187-spiritual-ascension-rote-1st-edition-m-taw?p=1239581#post1239581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's actually not. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> What the Spiritual Ascension spell does is make that transition without putting you in the Shadow, which is useful for the Gaolers since they'd hardly want to send their prey to a place that's also hostile to themselves while trying to make a capture.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Turning an object (or person) into Ephemera has the secondary effect of dumping said target into Twilight, at least (sort of like Disincorporation). In other words... transitioning into Ephemera puts said target &quot;in phase&quot; with the Twilight, or the Shadow, as desired.<br /> <br /> But, for sake of argument then, say the target Does stay in the Material plane... how does that affect the form for the purposes of Game Mechanics?<br /> <br /> Is the target to be treated like a Manifested spirit?<br /> Is the target shifted automatically into Twilight?<br /> As a Dreamspeaker, the mage can see in both Astral and Material simultaneously. Since the Astral is really just another phase of Twilight/Shadow... does that same effect function in this case?<br /> Can the mage shape themselves using Sculpt Ephemera?<br /> Can they heal themselves via Heal Spirits (whatever that Rote is called)?<br /> Is this a more proper way to interact with the Spirit Courts?<br /> <br /> Of course, if a mage is powerful enough to take this form, then they're certainly powerful enough to reach back into the Material to affect targets there.<br /> <br /> There are a LOT of mechanical questions going on here that the power does NOT explain...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","user":"DrKorpal","date":". 07-28-2018, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T07:35:19-07:00","id":1239673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrKorpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1239187-spiritual-ascension-rote-1st-edition-m-taw?p=1239669#post1239669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, all spirits - by the fact of being unaffected by gravity - can sort of hover at speed, and even &quot;fly&quot; to a height that is related either to rank or one of their attributes (ie.: finesse).All of that is in the Book of Spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope! Even in 1e:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BoS p90, &quot;Movement&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When considering movement, for the most part the same physical laws that govern the material world govern the Shadow, too. Gravity still exists, as do water currents and air vectors. Most spirits are roughly bound to the earth: a snake-spirit does not fly unless it has grown in strength by consuming the Essence of say, an eagle-spirit (at which point it may grow wings and be able to glide if not fly). The spirit of a shark is largely contained to its oceanic domain \u2014 after all, its body is built for swimming and that\u2019s where it finds the proper resonant Essence to consume.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T08:46:06-07:00","id":1239702,"title":"","content":"Also, the Shadow is a separate but tenuously connected alternative dimension to the reality that people naturally exist in, the same goes for the Astral. You do not enter them without a gateway, so they do not simply count as a phase the way Twilight does. The reason Dreamspeakers can witness the Astral and the Fallen simultaneously is because they break off a piece of their consciousness and use it to journey astrally. A Dreamspeaker can be having tea in London and battling a dragon in astral Tokyo. It\u2019s much closer to playing two different people than you seem to realize.<br /> <br /> If Fiery Transformation still allows for physical interaction beyond being on fire and Spiritual Ascension is supposed to be modeled on it then it stands to reason that SA also leaves you basically solid which means no Twilight. That doesn\u2019t seem likely though since ephemera isn\u2019t naturally solid. So like I said in an earlier post you probably transition to Twilight and then have to pay the Essence cost to maintain a physical form.<br /> <br /> Yes once you\u2019re made of ephemera you can be healed or shape-changed by Spirit. That\u2019s pretty obvious if you dig into the mechanics of other spells and draw some fairly simple conclusions.<br /> <br /> No it\u2019s not a more proper way to interact with Spirit courts, it\u2019s just a different way. You might be able to try deceiving spirits into thinking you\u2019re one of them, but probably only the Rank 0 spirits will buy it since they don\u2019t have a rank either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T10:23:37-07:00","id":1239726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1239187-spiritual-ascension-rote-1st-edition-m-taw?p=1239673#post1239673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope! Even in 1e:</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Book of Spirits</b> [pg. 132]<br /> <br /> <b>Speed</b>:<br /> Speed is equal to Power + Finesse + a \u201cspecies factor.\u201d Spirits that take human or animal form have a species factor equal to their earthly counterpart, although Rank 1 spirits, especially of normally immobile things, are often unaware that they can move. Spirits of inanimate objects usually have a species factor equal to 0, while spirits of more abstract forms generally have a species factor of 10. Vehicle spirits often have Acceleration traits equal to their material cousins, rather than a Speed trait (see the World of Darkness Rulebook, p. 142). To fnd the maximum<br /> Speed, add the spirit\u2019s Power + Finesse to the physical counterpart\u2019s maximum Speed.<br /> <br /> <b>In Twilight, all spirits (even spirits without apparent appendages) are considered to be able to move in just about any direction. Even those without \u201cwings\u201d or association with the concept of \ufb02ight (air elementals) can hover in any direction \u2014 though without a clear connection to the concept of \ufb02ight, they must hover within their Speed (in yards) off the ground, or at least a solid surface. For the most part, they are not bound by gravity, or suffer its effects </b>\u2014 you can\u2019t \u201cpush\u201d a murder spirit in Twilight down an elevator shaft. Materialized spirits are quite physical. They are affected by gravity, for example. They can still move about, per their Speed trait, but unless they have \u201cwings\u201d or some such, they cannot \ufb02y. Those that don\u2019t have wheels, legs, tentacles or treads, for example, are assumed to hover just off the ground.<br /> <br /> For those not meant to fly, there is an elevation limit... but only in Twilight or Shadow. The Movement section you listed is for <b>Manifested </b>spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","user":"DrKorpal","date":". 07-28-2018, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T21:16:26-07:00","id":1239892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrKorpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1239187-spiritual-ascension-rote-1st-edition-m-taw?p=1239726#post1239726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even those without \u201cwings\u201d or association with the concept of \ufb02ight (air elementals) can hover in any direction \u2014 though without a clear connection to the concept of \ufb02ight, they must hover within their Speed (in yards) off the ground, or at least a solid surface.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, precisely, did you think people would assume you meant by &quot;fly&quot; in the initial context of this discussion if not largely unfettered vertical movement?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T22:53:40-07:00","id":1240333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1239187-spiritual-ascension-rote-1st-edition-m-taw?p=1239892#post1239892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, precisely, did you think people would assume you meant by &amp;quot;fly&amp;quot; in the initial context of this discussion if not largely unfettered vertical movement?</div> </div> </div> </div>I presumed that someone answering the question would apply all aspects of the equation...<br /> <br /> This one rote implies a ridiculous amount of things - without actually explaining any of it.<br /> <br /> My presumption is that a mage taking Spirit form:<br /> 1) Is transformed from flesh to Ephemera.<br /> 2) Is shifted immediately into Twilight.<br /> 3) Can use the Spirit arcanum to alter their shape.<br /> 4) Is unaffected by gravity and, via shapeshifting, is fully capable of full flight.<br /> 5) Is capable of interacting with the Material world via the Spirit arcanum.<br /> 6) Is capable of crafting all of his/her material possessions (because all such objects are now also ephemera).<br /> 7) Can &quot;step sideways&quot; through the Gauntlet in either direction.<br /> 8) Can freely interact with Spirits, physically (and vice versa).<br /> 9) Can't be seen from the Material (without a supernatural power like Spirit Tongue or Auspex).<br /> 10) Can't be physically affected by beings in the Material (without supernatural powers involved).<br /> 11) Retains attributes/skills/rote effects as they were prior to transformation.<br /> <br /> <br /> But it sure would be nice to see an Official interpretation from the staff...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T23:24:29-07:00","id":1240336,"title":"","content":"Well you probably won't get it, they don't exactly lurk around on here just to pander to our questions, and especially not 1e questions.<br /> <br /> Besides, you appear to have a perfectly working level of understanding of what the likely consequences of using such a spell are already. Which is really all you need. You don't need an official interpretation.<br /> <br /> In fact, if -all- you want is an official interpretation from the staff then why the hell are you getting in an argument with Satchel who isn't staff? Just ignore them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-30-2018, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}